1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,740
She isn’t only acting.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,260
She’s already directing the camera.

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:06,920
Before she bends, she imagines

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,300
how the body will look.

5
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:10,840
The director recognizes the habit:

6
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,900
He once did the same thing

7
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,100
as an actor, carrying the frame

8
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,980
inside himself, managing every gesture

9
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:19,400
before anyone asked.

10
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:21,440
Then he names the alternative:

11
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,740
trust the collaboration.

12
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:25,740
An actor can think

13
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:26,540
about the image.

14
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:28,380
But when she must protect

15
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:31,020
the image alone, performance becomes

16
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:33,800
self-surveillance. So who is directing

17
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,000
whom—the filmmaker, the actor,

18
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,240
or the camera already living

19
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,640
inside both of them?
